# ==============================================================================
# CHANGES IN 0.4-dev65 (batch crash: "analysis stage exited -6" / MPSGraph)
# ==============================================================================
# Cause: with PARALLEL_ANALYSIS (since dev55) the CLAP embedding is computed in
# a background thread. When it finished, unload_clap() ran
# torch.mps.synchronize()/empty_cache() from that thread while the listening model
# was generating on the Apple GPU in the main thread (the singer-profile pass
# starts at that moment). MPS is not safe to clear from a second thread while
# another is using it, and macOS aborts the process: "Cannot form weak
# reference to instance ... of class MPSGraph ... over-released". It is a
# timing race, so the same song can pass on one run and crash on the next.
#  * GPU_CLEANUP_MAIN_THREAD_ONLY (default True): MPS cache clearing and the gc
#    sweeps around it only run on the main thread. The CLAP model is still
#    released in the background (CLAP runs on the CPU); the GPU cache is
#    cleared by the next main-thread unload.
#  * BATCH_RETRY_CRASHED_ANALYSIS (default True): if a track's analysis
#    process is killed by a crash (negative exit code), /batch retries that
#    track once in a fresh process instead of marking it failed.
# No analysis result changes. False on either restores dev64.

# ==============================================================================
# CHANGES IN 0.4-dev64 (the fixed layout is now on for every saved scan)
# ==============================================================================
# dev63's layout only applied when MOSS_CONSISTENT_REPORT was switched to True,
# and that setting was still False by default, so scans saved with the default
# settings kept whatever order the listening model wrote in (some opening with
# a prose description, some with "The duration of the piece is ...", fields
# missing or in a different order, no CHECKS block).
#
# New setting REPORT_FIXED_LAYOUT (default True). It is applied when the JSON
# is saved, after every analysis decision has been made, so it does not change
# the section map, timestamps, tempo, key, genre decision, singer identity or
# chat instructions. Every saved "analysis" now opens:
#   CHECKS (corrections to read before the report below):  (- lines, or none)
#   GENRE_RANKED, GENRE_ADJACENT, GENRE_RULED_OUT, KEY, TEMPO_BPM, CHORDS,
#   STRUCTURE, INSTRUMENTATION, DRUMS, TIMBRE, MOOD_VIBE, MELODICISM,
#   MELODIC_CONTOUR, MELODIC_RANGE, VOCALS_PRESENT, LEAD_VOCAL_CHARACTERISTICS,
#   LYRICS_PRESENT, LYRIC_SUBJECT, DESCRIPTION, REPORT_NOTE
# followed by the same sections as before (era, vocal, recommended structure).
# A field the model left out is filled from its first pass, else "uncertain".
# STRUCTURE= holds the measured section map (the same one as
# structure_sections), so the report can no longer disagree with the
# timestamps. The first pass is carried in the batch staging file so the
# two-process batch mode gets the same layout. Already laid-out text is left
# alone. False restores dev63 exactly.

