# CHANGES IN 0.4-dev53 (lyric timing retry for the section map)
# ==============================================================================
# * Comparing dev52 with dev46 on nine saved scans: boundary detection code
#   and detected boundaries are identical; the worse timestamps on recent
#   one verse-first pop test scan scans come from the scan inputs, chiefly the Whisper pass
#   that times the embedded lyrics. On every saved test scan it matched only
#   6-29% of the embedded lyrics with usable line timing, and the same file
#   gives the same result on every scan (greedy decoding). one verse-first pop test scan
#   came back as four "lines", one 0:00-2:05 of words not in the song.
# * The pass runs with no_repeat_ngram_size=4, which forbids any repeated
#   4-word phrase inside a 30-second window -- so repeated lyric lines cannot
#   be transcribed and Whisper writes something else instead. When the first
#   pass matches under 35% of the embedded lyrics, Whisper re-times them from
#   the isolated vocal stem and, if that still falls short, from the mix,
#   both without that rule. The best result is used only when it matches at
#   least 10 points more of the lyrics than the first pass; otherwise nothing
#   changes. Status lines say what happened. Tracks whose files carry no
#   usable lyrics (fewer than four lines) and the full-transcription path are
#   unaffected (WHISPER_TIMING_RETRY). Takes effect on new scans only.
# * Tried and rejected: placing the embedded lyric lines by the vocal stem's
#   notes alone. Without listening to the words it drifted by whole sections
#   (one verse-first pop test scan's verse 2 placed at 1:48) and made a pop test track and a multi-chorus test track
#   Love worse.
# Verified offline with a scripted Whisper (retry order, settings, keeping the
# first pass unless clearly beaten, errors); all nine saved scans replay as in
# dev52. With the setting off, dev53 behaves exactly as dev52.
#
# ==============================================================================
# CHANGES IN 0.4-dev52 (late bridge, final coda)
# ==============================================================================
# A dev51 rescan of one verse-first pop test scan came out "Verse 3 2:05-2:20 / Bridge
# 2:20-2:35 / Chorus 3 2:35-3:37" against the user's map "Bridge 1 2:05 /
# Bridge 2 2:20 / Chorus 2:35 / Chorus 2:50 / Outro 3:05-3:40":
# * 2:05-2:20 shares the verse backing (0.65-0.74 against the verses) but
#   drops to about half the drums (6.1 against 10-12) with the vocal about
#   2.5 semitones higher. The last of three or more occurrences of the verse
#   material, after two or more choruses and before the last one, with at most
#   0.6x the other occurrences' drum density and a vocal at least 1.5
#   semitones higher, is a Bridge, and keeps its own boundary against a
#   bridge that follows it (STRUCTURE_LATE_BRIDGE). one clean-replay test scan's Verse 3
#   (86% of the drums, slightly lower) is unaffected.
# * 3:04-3:33 matched the final chorus before it at only 0.24 (it was grouped
#   with the choruses through the post-chorus parts of earlier ones). The last
#   chorus, when its final part is not the same material as the rest of it and
#   nothing sung follows, ends where that part begins, and the part is the
#   Outro (STRUCTURE_FINAL_CODA). Only detected boundaries are used.
# That scan now replays: Intro / Verse 1 0:09 / Chorus 1 0:46 / Verse 2 1:06 /
# Chorus 2 1:32 / Bridge 1 2:05 / Bridge 2 2:20 / Chorus 3 2:35 / Outro 3:04.
