# ordinary chorus length), and the 0:09 verse start (vocal notes run from
# 0:09). The other eight saved scans replay exactly as in dev51; in 450
# jittered replays no run is worse than dev51. With both settings off, dev52
# behaves exactly as dev51.
#
# ==============================================================================
# CHANGES IN 0.4-dev51 (verse and chorus grouped as one part)
# ==============================================================================
# one verse-first pop test scan (both saved scans) and that arena-rock scan's dev49 scan still came out
# wrong in dev50 because parts were GROUPED wrongly before any naming:
# * one verse-first pop test scan: verse (0:08, 1:07) and chorus (0:45, 1:51, 2:35) share
#   their backing, so the grouping joined them -- although the choruses match
#   each other at 0.85-0.95 and the verses at 0.82, against 0.66 between the
#   two. When a group's own top split joins two such tighter halves (each
#   half at least STRUCTURE_COHESION_MARGIN more alike inside than across),
#   both halves are recurring sung material (two or more sung segments at
#   separate points), and one half sings mostly new words while the other's
#   mostly come back, the halves are kept apart and the new-words one is
#   treated as verse-like (STRUCTURE_SPLIT_BY_COHESION).
# * the arena-rock scan (dev49 scan): the 1:14 chorus was grouped only with a voiceless
#   stretch of the guitar solo that Whisper had filled with hallucinated
#   words. A sung segment grouped only with voiceless ones moves to the group
#   of sung parts it matches best (at the usual same-material level), unless
#   its words point the other way (STRUCTURE_LONE_SUNG_REGROUP).
# * A part heard once after the last chorus, straight after a chorus, whose
