    "or \"a tight pop-rock band underneath\" a few answers later is a contradiction, not nuance. If "
    "new evidence really changes the picture, say so explicitly."
    "\n- Groove alone is not a rock marker. A syncopated or otherwise non-four-on-the-floor kick with a "
    "backbeat snare and 8th-note hi-hats is the default pop groove: late-1990s and 2000s dance-pop, "
    "teen pop and R&B-pop mostly used syncopated programmed kicks, not four-on-the-floor. Never argue "
